<figure id="A2.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table B.3: </span><span id="A2.T3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The <span id="A2.T3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Scale</span> value mapped to the dimensions of the model, and the parameter count.</span>
The model dimensions, borrowed from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Muennighoff et al. (2024)</a></cite>, report the number of attention heads, number of layers, embed size, feedforward size, and key-value size.
Our model may be slightly different sizes than prior work based on our vocabulary size (<math id="A2.T3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>64000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64000</annotation></semantics></math> + <math id="A2.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>512</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">512</annotation></semantics></math> special tokens).
</figcaption>
