<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;">8</span>
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.8.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:341.4pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.8.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">de, en, fr, hi, ja, ru, vi, zh</span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.9" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;"><span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">12v0</span></span>
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;">12</span>
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.9.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:341.4pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.9.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">de, en, es, fr, hi, it, ja, pl, pt, ru, vi, zh</span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.10" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;"><span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">16v0</span></span>
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;">16</span>
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.10.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:341.4pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.10.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">de, en, es, fr, hi, id, it, ja, nl, pl, pt, ru, sv, tr, vi, zh</span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.11" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;"><span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">24v0</span></span>
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;">24</span>
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.11.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.11.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:341.4pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.11.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">cs, da, de, en, es, fa, fi, fr, hi, hu, id, it, ja, nl, pl, pt, ro, ru, sv, th, tr, uk, vi, zh</span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.12" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;"><span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">32v0</span></span>
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;">32</span>
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.12.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.12.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:341.4pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.12.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">ar, bg, ca, cs, da, de, el, en, es, fa, fi, fr, hi, hu, id, it, ja, ko, lt, nl, no, pl, pt, ro, ru, sk, sv, th, tr, uk, vi, zh</span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.13" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;"><span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">50v0</span></span>
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;">50</span>
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.13.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:3.0pt;padding-right:3.0pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.13.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:341.4pt;">
<span id="A2.T5.10.1.1.1.13.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">af, ar, ba, bm, bn, ca, ckb, cy, de, ee, el, en, es, fa, fil, fr, gn, gu, ha, he, hi, hr, id, it, ja, jv, kk, ko, mr, ms, my, nl, no, om, pl, ps, pt, ro, ru, sm, sv, sw, te, th, tr, uk, ur, vi, yo, zh</span>
</span></span></span>
</span></span></p>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#S5" title="5 The Curse of Multilinguality—Model Capacity Constraints ‣ ATLAS : Adaptive Transfer Scaling Laws for Multilingual Pretraining, Finetuning, and Decoding the Curse of Multilinguality" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> we aim to understand how a model’s capacity hinders multilingual learning—also termed the <em id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">curse of multilinguality</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Conneau et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chang et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.
To do this, we train models of various sizes, and with a range of language mixtures, shown in <a href="#A2.T5" title="In B.7.1 Multilingual Capacity Scaling Laws ‣ B.7 Experimental Details: Multilingual Capacity ‣ Appendix B Experimental Details ‣ Appendix ‣ ATLAS : Adaptive Transfer Scaling Laws for Multilingual Pretraining, Finetuning, and Decoding the Curse of Multilinguality" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>.
For simplicity, languages are always evenly sampled within their mixtures, even if some languages have more available text than others.
We train models on these mixtures, and evaluate the validation loss of all other languages, throughout training.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For a given target language <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> we have empirical loss scores across 11 differently sized models (from 10M to 8B), and across each mixture that contains the language in training, including monolingual, bilingual, and the multilingual mixtures shown in <a href="#A2.T5" title="In B.7.1 Multilingual Capacity Scaling Laws ‣ B.7 Experimental Details: Multilingual Capacity ‣ Appendix B Experimental Details ‣ Appendix ‣ ATLAS : Adaptive Transfer Scaling Laws for Multilingual Pretraining, Finetuning, and Decoding the Curse of Multilinguality" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We model each language’s loss as <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(N,D,K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(N,D,K)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is the model size, <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> are the number of training tokens for the <em id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">target</em> language, and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of languages in the training mixture (evenly sampled).
We define <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(N,D,K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(N,D,K)</annotation></semantics></math> as follows:</p>
<table id="A2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(N,D,K)\;=\;L_{\infty}\;+\;\frac{A\,K^{\phi}}{N^{\alpha}}\;+\;\frac{B\,K^{\psi}}{D^{\beta}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(N,D,K)\;=\;L_{\infty}\;+\;\frac{A\,K^{\phi}}{N^{\alpha}}\;+\;\frac{B\,K^{\psi}}{D^{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This law preserves the well-validated power-law behavior of monolingual scaling laws, while introducing <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> into both the capacity term (<math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AK^{\phi}/N^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AK^{\phi}/N^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>) and the data term (<math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="BK^{\psi}/D^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">BK^{\psi}/D^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>).
The exponent <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> captures how capacity requirements grow with the number of languages, while <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> captures how data requirements change with multilinguality: <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> indicates <em id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">positive transfer</em> (sublinear per-language data needs as <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> increases), <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi=0</annotation></semantics></math> implies no net transfer in the data term, and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> implies negative transfer/interference.
Under even sampling, the total tokens across languages are <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{tot}}=K\cdot D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{tot}}=K\cdot D</annotation></semantics></math>, in which case the data term can be rewritten as <math id="A2.SS7.SSS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\,K^{\psi+\beta}/D_{\mathrm{tot}}^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>tot</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\,K^{\psi+\beta}/D_{\mathrm{tot}}^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS7.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.7.2 </span>Adding languages: <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K*r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K*r</annotation></semantics></math></h5>

<div id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Practitioners may wish to change the number of languages supported by a model, from <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K*r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K*r</annotation></semantics></math>.
If the model size and training tokens remain unchanged, it will lead to a degradation in loss across languages, as the same compute budget is allocated across more languages.
When adding languages, the practitioner may wish to know how much they need to scale the model (<math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>) and the training compute <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> to maintain the same performance per language, as before.
We call this an <em id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">iso-loss</em>, as it approximately preserves the loss values, with a change in <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Compute-Optimality for <a href="#A2.E7" title="In B.7.1 Multilingual Capacity Scaling Laws ‣ B.7 Experimental Details: Multilingual Capacity ‣ Appendix B Experimental Details ‣ Appendix ‣ ATLAS : Adaptive Transfer Scaling Laws for Multilingual Pretraining, Finetuning, and Decoding the Curse of Multilinguality" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</h6>

<div id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As we increase <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K*r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K*r</annotation></semantics></math> we would like to understand the new <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N^{\prime},D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{\prime},D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> that <em id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">minimize</em> training compute on the iso-loss surface.
Let <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=K^{\prime}/K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=K^{\prime}/K</annotation></semantics></math>.
Minimizing <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}\propto N^{\prime}D^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}\propto N^{\prime}D^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> subject to</p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{A(Kr)^{\phi}}{N^{\prime\alpha}}+\frac{B(Kr)^{\psi}}{D^{\prime\beta}}\;=\;\frac{AK^{\phi}}{N^{\alpha}}+\frac{BK^{\psi}}{D^{\beta}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ψ</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{A(Kr)^{\phi}}{N^{\prime\alpha}}+\frac{B(Kr)^{\psi}}{D^{\prime\beta}}\;=\;\frac{AK^{\phi}}{N^{\alpha}}+\frac{BK^{\psi}}{D^{\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">yields the closed-form optimum:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Bigl(\tfrac{N^{\prime}}{N}\Bigr)^{\star}=r^{\phi/\alpha},\qquad\Bigl(\tfrac{D^{\prime}}{D}\Bigr)^{\star}=r^{\psi/\beta},\qquad\Bigl(\tfrac{D_{tot}^{\prime}}{D_{tot}}\Bigr)^{\star}=r^{1+\psi/\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigl(\tfrac{N^{\prime}}{N}\Bigr)^{\star}=r^{\phi/\alpha},\qquad\Bigl(\tfrac{D^{\prime}}{D}\Bigr)^{\star}=r^{\psi/\beta},\qquad\Bigl(\tfrac{D_{tot}^{\prime}}{D_{tot}}\Bigr)^{\star}=r^{1+\psi/\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">These expressions show a clear separation of roles: <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi/\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi/\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> governs the parameter burden of adding languages, whereas <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi/\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi/\beta</annotation></semantics></math> governs the data burden (with <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> reducing the per-language data requirement due to positive transfer).
Since the compute budget is in terms of total tokens <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{tot}}=K\cdot D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{tot}}=K\cdot D</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\propto ND_{\mathrm{tot}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\propto ND_{\mathrm{tot}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Adding languages: <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K*r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K*r</annotation></semantics></math> — Finding the compute multiplier.</h6>

<div id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At the iso-loss optimum, the compute multiplier is</p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{C^{\prime}}{C}\;=\;\frac{N^{\prime}D_{tot}^{\prime}}{ND_{tot}}\;=\;\Bigl(\tfrac{N^{\prime}}{N}\Bigr)^{\star}\Bigl(\tfrac{D^{\prime}_{\mathrm{tot}}}{D_{\mathrm{tot}}}\Bigr)^{\star}=r^{1+\phi/\alpha+\psi/\beta}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>C</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>tot</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{C^{\prime}}{C}\;=\;\frac{N^{\prime}D_{tot}^{\prime}}{ND_{tot}}\;=\;\Bigl(\tfrac{N^{\prime}}{N}\Bigr)^{\star}\Bigl(\tfrac{D^{\prime}_{\mathrm{tot}}}{D_{\mathrm{tot}}}\Bigr)^{\star}=r^{1+\phi/\alpha+\psi/\beta}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Intuitively, <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{\phi}{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>α</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{\phi}{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> measures the extra parameter capacity per added language, while <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{\psi}{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>ψ</mi><mi>β</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{\psi}{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> measures the extra (or reduced, if <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>) per-language token budget.
But since compute is defined with total tokens <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{tot}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{tot}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we consider the additional factor of <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> from enlarging the language inventory.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Adding languages: <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K*r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K*r</annotation></semantics></math> — Finding the Iso-loss curve.</h6>

<div id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\equiv\tfrac{N^{\prime}}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≡</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\equiv\tfrac{N^{\prime}}{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\equiv\tfrac{D^{\prime}}{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≡</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\equiv\tfrac{D^{\prime}}{D}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the multipliers for model size and (per-target-language) data when we grow the language inventory from <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\prime}=rK" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\prime}=rK</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define the baseline term contributions</p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{N}\;\equiv\;\frac{AK^{\phi}/N^{\alpha}}{AK^{\phi}/N^{\alpha}+BK^{\psi}/D^{\beta}},\qquad w_{D}\;=\;1-w_{N}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{N}\;\equiv\;\frac{AK^{\phi}/N^{\alpha}}{AK^{\phi}/N^{\alpha}+BK^{\psi}/D^{\beta}},\qquad w_{D}\;=\;1-w_{N}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The iso-loss condition equates the <em id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">sum of the two error terms</em> before and after the change in <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{A(Kr)^{\phi}}{(Ns)^{\alpha}}\;+\;\frac{B(Kr)^{\psi}}{(Dt)^{\beta}}\;=\;\frac{AK^{\phi}}{N^{\alpha}}\;+\;\frac{BK^{\psi}}{D^{\beta}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ψ</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{A(Kr)^{\phi}}{(Ns)^{\alpha}}\;+\;\frac{B(Kr)^{\psi}}{(Dt)^{\beta}}\;=\;\frac{AK^{\phi}}{N^{\alpha}}\;+\;\frac{BK^{\psi}}{D^{\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Dividing both sides by <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AK^{\phi}/N^{\alpha}+BK^{\psi}/D^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AK^{\phi}/N^{\alpha}+BK^{\psi}/D^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> yields the normalized <em id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">iso-loss constraint</em></p>
<table id="A2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\phi}\,w_{N}\,s^{-\alpha}\;+\;r^{\psi}\,w_{D}\,t^{-\beta}\;=\;1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn> 1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\phi}\,w_{N}\,s^{-\alpha}\;+\;r^{\psi}\,w_{D}\,t^{-\beta}\;=\;1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Solving for <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
Rearranging equation <a href="#A2.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ Adding languages: 𝐾 to 𝐾∗𝑟 — Finding the Iso-loss curve. ‣ B.7.2 Adding languages: 𝐾 to 𝐾∗𝑟 ‣ B.7 Experimental Details: Multilingual Capacity ‣ Appendix B Experimental Details ‣ Appendix ‣ ATLAS : Adaptive Transfer Scaling Laws for Multilingual Pretraining, Finetuning, and Decoding the Curse of Multilinguality" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\;=\;\left[\frac{r^{\psi}\,w_{D}}{1-r^{\phi}\,w_{N}\,s^{-\alpha}}\right]^{\!1/\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\;=\;\left[\frac{r^{\psi}\,w_{D}}{1-r^{\phi}\,w_{N}\,s^{-\alpha}}\right]^{\!1/\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The denominator must be positive, which implies the feasibility condition</p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\alpha}\;&gt;\;r^{\phi}\,w_{N}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">&gt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\alpha}\;&gt;\;r^{\phi}\,w_{N}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">As <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\alpha}\downarrow r^{\phi}w_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\alpha}\downarrow r^{\phi}w_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> the denominator tends to <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>; as <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, the denominator tends to <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to(r^{\psi}w_{D})^{1/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to(r^{\psi}w_{D})^{1/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Solving for <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
By symmetry,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\;=\;\left[\frac{r^{\phi}\,w_{N}}{1-r^{\psi}\,w_{D}\,t^{-\beta}}\right]^{\!1/\alpha},\qquad\text{with feasibility }\;t^{\beta}\;&gt;\;r^{\psi}\,w_{D}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>with feasibility </mtext><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">&gt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\;=\;\left[\frac{r^{\phi}\,w_{N}}{1-r^{\psi}\,w_{D}\,t^{-\beta}}\right]^{\!1/\alpha},\qquad\text{with feasibility }\;t^{\beta}\;&gt;\;r^{\psi}\,w_{D}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Total-token form.</span>
Under even sampling, <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{tot}}=KD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{tot}}=KD</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\prime}_{\mathrm{tot}}=K^{\prime}D^{\prime}=rKD^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>tot</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\prime}_{\mathrm{tot}}=K^{\prime}D^{\prime}=rKD^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, so</p>
<table id="A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{D^{\prime}_{\mathrm{tot}}}{D_{\mathrm{tot}}}\;=\;r\,\frac{D^{\prime}}{D}\;=\;r\left[\frac{r^{\psi}\,w_{D}}{1-r^{\phi}\,w_{N}\,s^{-\alpha}}\right]^{\!1/\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>tot</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{D^{\prime}_{\mathrm{tot}}}{D_{\mathrm{tot}}}\;=\;r\,\frac{D^{\prime}}{D}\;=\;r\left[\frac{r^{\psi}\,w_{D}}{1-r^{\phi}\,w_{N}\,s^{-\alpha}}\right]^{\!1/\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Compute-optimal frontier (starting from a compute-optimal <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(K,N,D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(K,N,D)</annotation></semantics></math>).</span>
Suppose the <em id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p5.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">baseline</em> <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(K,N,D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(K,N,D)</annotation></semantics></math> is compute-optimal for its loss level, i.e., it minimizes <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\propto ND" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\propto ND</annotation></semantics></math> subject to <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AK^{\phi}/N^{\alpha}+BK^{\psi}/D^{\beta}=\text{const}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>const</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AK^{\phi}/N^{\alpha}+BK^{\psi}/D^{\beta}=\text{const}</annotation></semantics></math>. A standard Lagrange multiplier argument then yields</p>
<table id="A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha\,\frac{AK^{\phi}}{N^{\alpha}}\;=\;\beta\,\frac{BK^{\psi}}{D^{\beta}}\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad w_{N}\;=\;\frac{\beta}{\alpha+\beta},\;\;\;w_{D}\;=\;\frac{\alpha}{\alpha+\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mi>β</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msup></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="1.007em">,</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\,\frac{AK^{\phi}}{N^{\alpha}}\;=\;\beta\,\frac{BK^{\psi}}{D^{\beta}}\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad w_{N}\;=\;\frac{\beta}{\alpha+\beta},\;\;\;w_{D}\;=\;\frac{\alpha}{\alpha+\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">After changing <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\to rK" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\to rK</annotation></semantics></math>, the compute along the iso-loss curve is <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}/C=s\,t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}/C=s\,t</annotation></semantics></math> (or <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}/C=s\cdot\tfrac{D^{\prime}_{\mathrm{tot}}}{D_{\mathrm{tot}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>tot</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}/C=s\cdot\tfrac{D^{\prime}_{\mathrm{tot}}}{D_{\mathrm{tot}}}</annotation></semantics></math> if compute is defined with total tokens).
Minimizing this product subject to equation <a href="#A2.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ Adding languages: 𝐾 to 𝐾∗𝑟 — Finding the Iso-loss curve. ‣ B.7.2 Adding languages: 𝐾 to 𝐾∗𝑟 ‣ B.7 Experimental Details: Multilingual Capacity ‣ Appendix B Experimental Details ‣ Appendix ‣ ATLAS : Adaptive Transfer Scaling Laws for Multilingual Pretraining, Finetuning, and Decoding the Curse of Multilinguality" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> again via Lagrange multipliers gives the stationarity condition</p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\,r^{\phi}\,w_{N}\,s^{-\alpha}\;=\;\beta\,r^{\psi}\,w_{D}\,t^{-\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\,r^{\phi}\,w_{N}\,s^{-\alpha}\;=\;\beta\,r^{\psi}\,w_{D}\,t^{-\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p5.3" class="ltx_p">Combining with equation <a href="#A2.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ Adding languages: 𝐾 to 𝐾∗𝑟 — Finding the Iso-loss curve. ‣ B.7.2 Adding languages: 𝐾 to 𝐾∗𝑟 ‣ B.7 Experimental Details: Multilingual Capacity ‣ Appendix B Experimental Details ‣ Appendix ‣ ATLAS : Adaptive Transfer Scaling Laws for Multilingual Pretraining, Finetuning, and Decoding the Curse of Multilinguality" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> and substituting the compute-optimal weights above yields the <em id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p5.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">unique</em> minimum-compute point on the new frontier:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Bigl(\tfrac{N^{\prime}}{N}\Bigr)^{\star}\!=r^{\phi/\alpha},\qquad\Bigl(\tfrac{D^{\prime}}{D}\Bigr)^{\star}\!=r^{\psi/\beta},\qquad\Bigl(\tfrac{D^{\prime}_{\mathrm{tot}}}{D_{\mathrm{tot}}}\Bigr)^{\star}\!=r^{\,1+\psi/\beta}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>tot</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>tot</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn> 1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigl(\tfrac{N^{\prime}}{N}\Bigr)^{\star}\!=r^{\phi/\alpha},\qquad\Bigl(\tfrac{D^{\prime}}{D}\Bigr)^{\star}\!=r^{\psi/\beta},\qquad\Bigl(\tfrac{D^{\prime}_{\mathrm{tot}}}{D_{\mathrm{tot}}}\Bigr)^{\star}\!=r^{\,1+\psi/\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p5.4" class="ltx_p">At this point each error component is <em id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p5.4.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">individually restored</em> to its baseline magnitude:
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(Kr)^{\phi}/N^{\prime\alpha}=AK^{\phi}/N^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(Kr)^{\phi}/N^{\prime\alpha}=AK^{\phi}/N^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(Kr)^{\psi}/D^{\prime\beta}=BK^{\psi}/D^{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ψ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">′</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>ψ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(Kr)^{\psi}/D^{\prime\beta}=BK^{\psi}/D^{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>,
so the weights <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(w_{N},w_{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(w_{N},w_{D})</annotation></semantics></math>—and hence the balance of capacity/data bottlenecks—remain unchanged. Because the frontier is convex in <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\log s,\log t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\log s,\log t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS7.SSS2.Px3.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log C^{\prime}=\log s+\log t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log C^{\prime}=\log s+\log t</annotation></semantics></math> is linear, this stationary point is the global compute minimum along the iso-loss curve.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
